# Engram — Config Profile: Personal AI Agent Memory (server-bootstrap env)
# Shape: high-value, low-volume single-agent memory — recall of a rare-but-
#        critical fact matters more than raw precision (召回 > 精确).
#
# This file is the SERVER-BOOTSTRAP env layer for this profile. Its ranking /
# dedup values MIRROR this directory's config.yaml so the process starts up
# already tuned toward this profile; see ./config.yaml and ./README.md for the
# full rationale and the runtime-applied knobs.
#
# NOTE — YAML-only knobs are NOT here. min_score, rerank_enabled, limit, ttl,
# and every field marked "# proposed" in config.yaml (per_type_min_importance,
# etc.) have NO ENGRAM_* env equivalent. They live only in config.yaml and are
# applied at runtime via the memory_apply_config MCP tool — not at startup.
#
# Every ENGRAM_* name below is spelled exactly as in docs/configuration.md and
# carries its code-derived default source. Copy to .env and fill in your values.

# ── Storage ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What: Qdrant endpoint over gRPC (6334). Default: localhost:6334 (config.go).
ENGRAM_QDRANT_URL=localhost:6334

# ── Embedding ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What: embedding provider. Default: openai (config.go).
ENGRAM_EMBEDDER_PROVIDER=openai
# What: OpenAI API key for embeddings. Default: "" (config.go). Placeholder only — never a real key.
ENGRAM_OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# What: embedding model name. Default: text-embedding-3-small (config.go).
ENGRAM_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
# What: embedding vector dimension. Default: 1536 (config.go).
ENGRAM_EMBEDDING_DIMENSION=1536

# ── Transport ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What: which servers to run; "both" = MCP + HTTP. Default: stdio (config.go).
ENGRAM_TRANSPORT=both
# What: HTTP listen port. Default: 8080 (config.go).
ENGRAM_HTTP_PORT=8080
# What: bearer token for the HTTP API. Default: "" (config.go). Placeholder only.
ENGRAM_API_KEY=replace-with-a-random-secret

# ── Ranking / Dedup — mirrors this profile's config.yaml ───────────────────────
# What: relevance weight; semantic match is primary. Default: 1.0 (config.go). = config.yaml relevance_weight.
ENGRAM_WEIGHT_RELEVANCE=1.0
# What: recency weight. Default: 0.5 (config.go). Lowered to 0.20 so old identity
#   facts do not sink beneath fresh noise — recall of rare-but-critical facts wins.
ENGRAM_WEIGHT_RECENCY=0.20
# What: importance weight. Default: 0.3 (config.go). Raised to 0.35 to keep rare
#   high-value memories surfaced in a low-volume store.
ENGRAM_WEIGHT_IMPORTANCE=0.35
# What: enable per-type admission (dedup / importance clamp / rate limit). Default: false (config.go).
#   ON here so the per-type dedup thresholds below take effect.
ENGRAM_AMAC_ENABLED=true
# What: global dedup threshold. Default: 0.92 (config.go). Conservative 0.92 —
#   only block near-exact duplicates; keep distinct nuances of a rare fact.
ENGRAM_DEDUP_THRESHOLD=0.92
# What: identity dedup threshold. Default: 0.95 (dedup.go). Almost never merge a
#   self/owner fact — update deliberately, don't silently fold.
ENGRAM_DEDUP_THRESHOLD_IDENTITY=0.95
# What: directive dedup threshold. Default: 0.90 (dedup.go). Avoids sycophancy-flywheel
#   fragmentation of "user prefers X".
ENGRAM_DEDUP_THRESHOLD_DIRECTIVE=0.90
# What: insight dedup threshold. Default: 0.92 (dedup.go). Conservative — keep nuances.
ENGRAM_DEDUP_THRESHOLD_INSIGHT=0.92
# What: event dedup threshold. Default: 0.92 (dedup.go). Conservative — low volume, no pile-up risk.
ENGRAM_DEDUP_THRESHOLD_EVENT=0.92
